; Stage 15 W9 item 9's other boundary, and the one that pins WHICH rule was
; chosen: `i1` is a bool over {0, 1}, not a 1-bit two's complement integer.
; Reading it as the latter gives the range [-1, 0], which would accept -1 here
; and reject `1` — the value `true` denotes — so this fixture fails if the
; width-1 arm is ever "fixed" by letting it fall through to the signed branch.
;
; Compiling this must FAIL with:
;   "defvar: integer literal -1 does not fit i1"
(defvar w9i1-neg:i1 -1)

(defn main ():i32
  (return 0))
